Engineering Rationale

Engineering Need

Adaptive vehicle intelligence requires more than the acquisition of observations. The system must establish the operational meaning and relationships of those observations before appropriate adaptive decisions can be generated.

---

Engineering Context

SO-F-003 occupies the interpretation stage between environmental perception and adaptive decision generation.

SO-F-002 provides observations of relevant conditions. SO-F-003 transforms those observations into an interpreted operating context that can be used by subsequent decision-making functions.

---

Engineering Justification

Separating interpretation from perception preserves the distinction between observing conditions and understanding their operational significance.

Separating interpretation from decision generation likewise prevents the system from coupling contextual understanding with action selection.

This separation supports modular architecture, clearer verification boundaries, independent evolution of interpretation capabilities, and improved traceability of decisions to the contextual information from which they originate.

---

Expected Engineering Benefit

Achievement of this objective enables the system to:

- Establish meaningful operational context from available observations.
- Maintain awareness of changing situations.
- Provide contextual information to downstream decision functions.
- Preserve separation between observation, interpretation, decision, and execution.
- Support traceable adaptive decision-making.

---

Dependencies and Assumptions

This objective depends directly on the observational capability established by SO-F-002.

Its outputs are expected to support SO-F-004 and other functions requiring an interpreted operating context.

Interpretation may operate under incomplete or uncertain observations and shall therefore support appropriate representation of uncertainty without transferring decision authority into this objective.
